From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:36:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/display/dp: read a converter's frame sequential to frame
 packing capability

The detailed capabilities of an HDMI downstream facing port carry, in
byte 3, bit 0, DP_DS_HDMI_FRAME_SEQ_TO_FRAME_PACK (drm_dp.h): the
protocol converter can turn a DisplayPort frame-sequential stereo stream,
whose eyes MSA MISC1 names, into HDMI frame packing. AMD's Display Core
reads it into is_dp_hdmi_s3d_converter for HDMI and DP++ downstream ports
alike ("process DP++ case as HDMI case according DP1.4 spec",
link_dp_capability.c) and names the stream format
TIMING_3D_FORMAT_DP_HDMI_INBAND_FA, "Inband FA to HDMI Frame Pack ... for
active DP-HDMI dongle"; NVIDIA defines the same bit as
NV_DPCD_DETAILED_CAP_INFO_FRAME_SEQ_TO_FRAME_PACK. No helper reads it.

Add drm_dp_downstream_frame_seq_to_frame_pack(), shaped like
drm_dp_downstream_420_passthrough(): a branch device with detailed
capability information, an HDMI or DP++ downstream port, and the bit.
Drivers can then offer the converter's frame packing for
frame-sequential streams where the converter declares it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.h     |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c
index 6db2cbe56..912cbfea0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c
@@ -1558,6 +1558,38 @@ bool drm_dp_downstream_444_to_420_conversion(const u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE]
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(drm_dp_downstream_444_to_420_conversion);
 
+/**
+ * drm_dp_downstream_frame_seq_to_frame_pack() - determine downstream facing port
+ *                                               frame sequential to frame
+ *                                               packing conversion capability
+ * @dpcd: DisplayPort configuration data
+ * @port_cap: downstream facing port capabilities
+ *
+ * An HDMI downstream facing port (or a DP++ one, read the same way) may turn a
+ * frame-sequential stereo stream, the eye of each frame named by MSA MISC1,
+ * into HDMI frame packing.
+ *
+ * Returns: whether the downstream facing port declares that conversion
+ */
+bool drm_dp_downstream_frame_seq_to_frame_pack(const u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE],
+					       const u8 port_cap[4])
+{
+	if (!drm_dp_is_branch(dpcd))
+		return false;
+
+	if ((dpcd[DP_DOWNSTREAMPORT_PRESENT] & DP_DETAILED_CAP_INFO_AVAILABLE) == 0)
+		return false;
+
+	switch (port_cap[0] & DP_DS_PORT_TYPE_MASK) {
+	case DP_DS_PORT_TYPE_HDMI:
+	case DP_DS_PORT_TYPE_DP_DUALMODE:
+		return port_cap[3] & DP_DS_HDMI_FRAME_SEQ_TO_FRAME_PACK;
+	default:
+		return false;
+	}
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(drm_dp_downstream_frame_seq_to_frame_pack);
+
 /**
  * drm_dp_downstream_rgb_to_ycbcr_conversion() - determine downstream facing port
  *                                               RGB->YCbCr conversion capability
diff --git a/include/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.h b/include/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.h
index 27bf28575..df89ff648 100644
--- a/include/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.h
+++ b/include/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.h
@@ -738,6 +738,8 @@ bool drm_dp_downstream_420_passthrough(const u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE],
 				       const u8 port_cap[4]);
 bool drm_dp_downstream_444_to_420_conversion(const u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE],
 					     const u8 port_cap[4]);
+bool drm_dp_downstream_frame_seq_to_frame_pack(const u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE],
+					       const u8 port_cap[4]);
 struct drm_display_mode *drm_dp_downstream_mode(struct drm_device *dev,
 						const u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE],
 						const u8 port_cap[4]);
-- 
